  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In a steady state, the inductor behaves as a conducting wire. So, the equivalent circuit becomes,&nbsp;<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/6f1e20ab-e364-407e-932b-11e5067c294b-image.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 246px;\" /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p><p>so, the circuit becomes,&nbsp;<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/7f827bc9-02b6-4b67-bd1d-5805a0893550-image.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 195px;\" /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>30</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></p>",
